# Android signing material — NEVER commit (rotated 2026-06-01 after the old
# key + passwords leaked via git history; see project memory). Keep local-only.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
# relay.properties holds the relay .onion. It now comes from the environment
# (RELAY_ONION_URL); a local relay.properties is an optional, gitignored dev
# fallback (env var takes precedence). See relay.properties.example.
relay.properties
# Firebase client config (FCM vendor-push tier — notification-levels-plan.md
# §2b). Client config, not a secret, but kept out of git the same way as
# keystore.properties: present locally, absent on fresh clones/CI. The
# google-services Gradle plugin is applied with missingGoogleServicesStrategy
# = IGNORE plus a per-variant guard (androidApp/build.gradle.kts): RELEASE
# builds fail loudly when the file is absent/invalid (never silently ship
# without Firebase config); debug builds warn and continue (CI runs unit
# suites without the file; such a debug APK just has FCM unconfigured).
# Split by build type so debug resolves the DEV Firebase project and release
# resolves PROD automatically (no manual swap): src/debug = dev,
# src/release = prod.
androidApp/src/*/google-services.json
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
/.idea/
/.kotlin/
/.claude/
/iosApp/build/
/iosApp/run/
/run/
/e2e-tests/node_modules/
# package-lock.json is NOT ignored. Every
# devDependency here uses a `^` range, so an ignored lockfile meant a fresh
# clone resolved a completely unpinned Appium/WDIO toolchain — the one unpinned
# surface in an otherwise checksum-pinned build (Gradle dependency verification,
# vendored Argon2, pinned tor.xcframework), and one that gets device-level shell
# access via `relaxedSecurity`. Commit the lockfile and install with `npm ci`.
/e2e-tests/build/
# Local test relay's crash-resume journal.
/e2e-tests/.local-relay-state.json
/e2e-tests/.local-relay-state.json.corrupt
# Local-only security review notes and planning files. They describe findings
# before they are fixed and must never be committed or pushed.
SECURITY_AUDIT.md
*-security-audit*.txt
code-review*.txt
SECURITY_REVIEW*.md
notification-implementation-plan.txt
docs/*-security-audit-prompt.txt

# graphify knowledge-graph output (generated)
graphify-out/

# fastlane runtime artifacts (metadata trees ARE committed; these are not)
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots
fastlane/test_output
fastlane/*.p8
fastlane/*service-account*.json
fastlane/.env*

# Device-extraction AFU test captures (security-tests/device-extraction/):
# adb backups, memory/logcat dumps, screenshots, and search results all
# contain real seeded PINs/passphrases/canary plaintext and must never be
# committed. See security-tests/device-extraction/RUNBOOK.md.
/security-tests/device-extraction/out/
